==Enemy==
Just like his counterparts, he sports long range, health, and damage to some extent. He also has a new trick up his sleeve: his attacks have a moderate chance to slow down your cats. Thanks to this ability, the battle against him can be substantially longer compared to fighting his other variants.

==Strategy==
Don't be fooled by his low stats. At his first appearance, depending on your anti-alien treasures, he is buffed to 400% minimum, making his battle exponentially longer, especially accounting for the [[Cyberhorn]]s in his debut stage. If you have anything that has above 600 range, such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]], use it. Later on, you can just treat this as a stronger version of normal [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]].

